```php
<?php
require 'vendor/autoload.php'; // If using composer for Redis library
use Predis\Client as Redis; 

$client = new Redis([
    'scheme' => 'tcp',
    'host'   => 'localhost',
    'port'   => 6379,
]);

class UserUpdater {
    private $db; // Database connection
    private $redisClient; // Redis client

    public function __construct($pdo) {
        $this->db = $pdo;
        $this->redisClient = new Redis();
    }

    public function updateProfile($userId, $ipAddress, $status){
        // Acquire lock to prevent concurrent updates for the same user
        $lockKey = "profileUpdate:${userId}";
        $this->redisClient->setnx($lockKey, 1);

        if (!$this->checkRateLimit($ipAddress)) {
            $this->logToAudit("Rate limit exceeded for IP ${ipAddress}");
            throw new Exception('You have exceeded the rate limit. Please try again later.');
        }

        $updateQuery = "UPDATE `USER_TABLE` SET status=?, last_modified_ip=?, last_modified_date=NOW() WHERE id=? ";
        $stmt = $this->db->prepare($updateQuery);
        $result = $stmt->execute([$status, $ipAddress, $userId]);

        if ($result){
            $auditMsg = "User ID ${userId} updated. Status: ${status}, IP: ${ipAddress}";
            // Release lock after the update has been done
            $this->redisClient->del($lockKey);
            $this->logToAudit($auditMsg);
        } else {
            throw new Exception('Failed to update user profile.');
        }
    }

    private function checkRateLimit($ipAddress){
        $key = "update_attempts:${ipAddress}";

        // Check if the IP address has made more than 10 attempts in the last hour
        $currentCount = $this->redisClient->get($key);
        if ($currentCount >= 10) {
            return false;
        }

        // Increment the count for this IP and set expiration time to one hour 
        $this->redisClient->incr($key);
        $this->redisClient->expire($key, 3600);

        return true;
    }

    private function logToAudit($message){
        // Insert audit log to DB (assuming 'audit_log' table exists)
        $query = "INSERT INTO `AUDIT_TABLE` (event, timestamp) VALUES (?, NOW())";
        $stmt = $this->db->prepare($query);
        $stmt->execute([$message]);
    }
}
?>
```
In this script, we first check if there is a lock for the user in Redis. If there is no lock, then we proceed with updating the profile and logging the audit event. We use Redis as our rate limiting mechanism: every time an update attempt is made from a specific IP address, it increments a counter in Redis associated with that IP. If this count exceeds 10 (you can adjust according to your need), then we reject further updates from this IP for the next hour. After successfully updating the user profile and logging the event, we release the lock so other requests can be processed.
']

