If special_flag is set, we do not use the records array after initializing it; thus, we should call free to release the allocated memory before the function ends. If use_random is set, each record's value is initialized with a random number; otherwise, it is set to specific_value. This approach ensures efficient memory management and error handling under different operational conditions. 

