```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <stdatomic.h>
#include <pthread.h>

#define MAX_PDUS 100
#define MAX_LENGTH 1500

typedef struct LTE_MAC_PDU {
    // your MAC CE and LCR fields here
} LTE_MAC_PDU;

LTE_MAC_PDU* PDUs[MAX_PDUS];
atomic_int num_PDUs = 0;
pthread_mutex_t lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

LTE_MAC_PDU* create_and_populate_PDU() {
    LTE_MAC_PDU* pdu = malloc(sizeof(LTE_MAC_PDU));
    // populate MAC CE and LCR fields here, ensure length <= MAX_LENGTH
    return pdu;
}

void populate_PDUs() {
    while (1) {
        if (atomic_load(&num_PDUs) >= MAX_PDUS) break;

        // Acquire lock to prevent data corruption in concurrent access.
        pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);

        // Check again after acquiring lock.
        if (atomic_load(&num_PDUs) < MAX_PDUS) {
            PDUs[atomic_fetch_add(&num_PDUs, 1)] = create_and_populate_PDU();
        }

        // Release lock to allow other threads.
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
    }
}
```
This implementation uses a simple mutex lock to synchronize access to the shared `num_PDUs` variable, ensuring thread safety and avoiding data corruption in concurrent access scenarios. The `atomic_load()` function is used instead of directly reading from `num_PDUs` inside the critical section to ensure that all memory operations have completed before they are made visible to other threads.

Please replace `// your MAC CE and LCR fields here`, `// populate MAC CE and LCR fields here, ensure length <= MAX_LENGTH` with actual logic for creating and populating PDUs. 

