response:
['Here's a C# solution using the HttpClient class to send POST requests, and Newtonsoft.Json for handling JSON responses. It also uses Polly library for retrying failed HTTP requests with exponential backoff. 

This is not executable code but will give you an idea of how it could be implemented. You'll need to install `Newtonsoft.Json` and `Polly` NuGet packages in your project before using the following solution.

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Net.Http;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using Newtonsoft.Json;
using Polly;

public class DataSender
{
    private readonly HttpClient _httpClient = new HttpClient();
    private const string ApiKeyHeaderName = "api-key";
    private readonly JsonSerializerSettings _jsonSerializerSettings = new JsonSerializerSettings { TypeNameHandling = TypeNameHandling.Auto };

    public DataSender(string apiKey, Uri serverUri)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(apiKey)) throw new ArgumentException("Api key can't be null or empty", nameof(apiKey));
        _httpClient.BaseAddress = serverUri ?? throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(serverUri));
        _httpClient.DefaultRequestHeaders.Add(ApiKeyHeaderName, apiKey);
    }

    public async Task<JsonResponse> SendDataAsync(byte[] data)
    {
        var policy = Policy
            .Handle<HttpRequestException>()
            .WaitAndRetryAsync(3, retryAttempt => TimeSpan.FromSeconds(Math.Pow(2, retryAttempt)));

        try
        {
            using (var content = new ByteArrayContent(data))
            using (var response = await policy.ExecuteAsync(() => _httpClient.PostAsync("", content)))
            {
                if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;

                var jsonString = await response.Content.ReadAsStringAsync();
                LogRequestAndResponse(data, jsonString);
                return JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<JsonResponse>(jsonString, _jsonSerializerSettings);
            }
        }
        catch (Exception e)
        {
            Console.WriteLine(e); // log error
            throw;
        }
    }

    private void LogRequestAndResponse(byte[] requestData, string responseJson)
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Request data:");
        Console.WriteLine(Convert.ToBase64String(requestData));

        Console.WriteLine("Response data:");
        Console.WriteLine(responseJson);
    }
}
``` 

This class encapsulates the HTTP client and API key. When an instance of this class is created, it's expected to have a valid API key and server URI as arguments. It uses Polly library for retrying failed requests with exponential backoff up to 3 times. The method `LogRequestAndResponse` logs request data and response in base64 encoded format before sending them to the remote server and after receiving a response respectively.
']

