To log errors or warnings, the program opens and closes a file handle every time it logs something (as a simple demonstration). A better approach might be to pass around a FILE* pointer instead of opening and closing the file on each call. The filename for logging is also hardcoded as "logfile.txt".

```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
